(Basel III: International Regulatory Framework for Banks) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Basel Committee on Banking Supervision) Tj
T*
(Basel III: A global regulatory framework for more resilient banks and banking systems) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Executive Summary) Tj
T*
(Basel III is an international regulatory framework developed by the Basel Committee on) Tj
T*
(Banking Supervision in response to the financial crisis of 2007-2009. The framework) Tj
T*
(strengthens bank capital requirements, introduces new regulatory requirements on bank) Tj
T*
(liquidity and leverage, and aims to improve the banking sector's ability to absorb) Tj
T*
(shocks arising from financial and economic stress.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Capital Requirements) Tj
T*
(2.1 Enhanced Capital Quality) Tj
T*
(Basel III emphasizes the quality of capital, with a greater focus on Common Equity Tier) Tj
T*
(1 \(CET1\) capital. CET1 capital must be loss-absorbing on a going-concern basis.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2.2 Minimum Capital Ratios) Tj
T*
(- Common Equity Tier 1 \(CET1\): 4.5% of risk-weighted assets) Tj
T*
(- Tier 1 Capital: 6.0% of risk-weighted assets) Tj
T*
(- Total Capital: 8.0% of risk-weighted assets) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2.3 Capital Conservation Buffer) Tj
T*
(Banks must maintain a capital conservation buffer of 2.5% of risk-weighted assets,) Tj
T*
(comprising CET1 capital. The buffer is designed to ensure banks build up capital buffers) Tj
T*
(during normal times that can be drawn down in periods of stress.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2.4 Countercyclical Capital Buffer) Tj
T*
(The countercyclical buffer ranges from 0% to 2.5% of risk-weighted assets and is) Tj
T*
(activated by national authorities based on credit conditions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Leverage Ratio) Tj
T*
(3.1 Minimum Requirement) Tj
T*
(Basel III introduces a minimum leverage ratio of 3% of total exposures. The leverage) Tj
T*
(ratio is calculated as Tier 1 capital divided by the bank's total exposures.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.2 Purpose) Tj
T*
(The leverage ratio serves as a non-risk-based backstop to the risk-based capital) Tj
T*
(requirements and helps contain the build-up of excessive leverage in the banking system.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Liquidity Standards) Tj
T*
(4.1 Liquidity Coverage Ratio \(LCR\)) Tj
T*
(The LCR requires banks to hold sufficient high-quality liquid assets to cover net cash) Tj
T*
(outflows over a 30-day stress period. The minimum requirement is 100%.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4.2 Net Stable Funding Ratio \(NSFR\)) Tj
T*
(The NSFR requires banks to maintain a stable funding profile relative to the composition) Tj
T*
(of their assets and off-balance sheet activities. The minimum requirement is 100%.) Tj
ET
endstream
