(Studies indicate that Basel III implementation will lead to a more resilient banking) Tj
T*
(system with a modest impact on long-term economic growth.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(10.2 Transition Costs) Tj
T*
(Banks may face transition costs in adjusting their business models and capital) Tj
T*
(structures to meet the new requirements.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(11. Future Revisions) Tj
T*
(11.1 Ongoing Review) Tj
T*
(The Basel Committee continues to review and refine the regulatory framework based on) Tj
T*
(experience and emerging risks.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(11.2 Basel IV) Tj
T*
(Further revisions to the Basel framework, sometimes referred to as Basel IV, are under) Tj
T*
(consideration to address remaining weaknesses.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(12. Conclusion) Tj
T*
(Basel III represents a comprehensive reform of the global regulatory framework for) Tj
T*
(banks. By strengthening capital, liquidity, and leverage standards, the framework aims) Tj
T*
(to promote a more resilient banking sector that supports sustainable economic growth.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Basel Committee on Banking Supervision) Tj
T*
(Bank for International Settlements) Tj
T*
(CH-4002 Basel, Switzerland) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
